  "notes": "The late-90s/early-00s radio-rock centre: 75–128 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature singles at 84–120. Three drum deltas come from the entry — \"kick 1 and the '&' of 3\", \"snare 2&4 struck hard\" (a high accent tier with a tight ghost), and \"8th hat in verse and open hat in chorus\" — and the fourth stated fact is an arrangement device that the model encodes as one: \"the 'drop everything but the vocal for one bar' device before the last chorus\" is `dropOutBeats` at 0.95 over 4 beats. The kit is \"mixed dry and forward\", which is why the velocity tier is loud rather than soft even though the humanize is loose. Harmony is a major/minor mixture — vi–IV–I–V and i–III–VII–VI — with \"a suspended 2nd ringing through changes\" from the open-tuned and capo'd shapes, so the sus substitution is authored. The melody is \"rasped in a narrow mid-range with the hook on a repeated pitch\", i.e. a narrow register with a low motif pitch count and a `riff_loop` structure, and the \"harmony vocals only on the chorus\" is the modest counter ratio. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so and marks the harmonic claims **[LOW-CONF]** as convention-based, which is why `keys` is left inherited. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 102.",
